{title: Enthroned on Our Praises}
{artist: Brenton Dowdy}
{key: D}

{comment: Verse}
[Em] Let the song we [D/F#]sing be an overflowing [A]theme
From the bottom of our hearts we lift You [Em]up
You’re the [D/F#]name above all [A]names
[Em] Let the praise we [D/F#]bring be an overflowing [A]spring
Where the waters never run out or [Em]dry up
Enthrone Your [D/F#]presence on our [A]praise
[Em] Enthrone Your [D/F#]presence on our [A]praise

{comment: Chorus}
[G] There is one [A]victory, there is one [Bm]song
We will [F#m]sing it, we will sing it to You
[G] There is one [A]kingdom, there is one [Bm]throne
You will bring [F#m]it, You will bring it as we [G]sing

{comment: Bridge}
[G] We lift You up, Your [A]kingdom comes down [Bm]
We sing Your praise, we see Your [D/F#]glory all [G]around
We shout Your name and we [A]tremble at the [Em]sound
[D/F#] You are [G]enthroned on our [A]praises
